subgraph PCHIPSEC["5 · Pchip — Fritsch-Carlson 1980 monotone cubic Hermite · Pchip.cs"]
    direction TB

    P0["<b>Why PCHIP and not a natural cubic spline.</b><br/>Pchip.cs:9-13<br/>· no overshoot between data points<br/>· no Runge phenomenon<br/>· C1 continuous — value and 1st derivative<br/>· extrema sit AT KNOTS; between knots the<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;cubic is monotone<br/><br/>An overshooting spline would invent motion<br/>the source never had, and the extrema<br/>detector would then chase phantom<br/>turning points."]

    P1["<b>Fit x, y, count</b>  :64-84<br/>validate x STRICTLY increasing :73-75<br/>Array.Copy into owned storage :79-80<br/>_n = count<br/>-> ComputeTangents<br/><br/>reuses existing arrays; the live steppers<br/>refit four of these per bone per frame, so<br/>allocating here would dominate GC cost"]

    P2["<b>Secant slopes</b>  :182-183<br/>d[i] = y[i+1] - y[i] / x[i+1] - x[i]"]

    P3{"n == 2 ?<br/>:187"}
    P4["m[0] = m[1] = d[0]  :190<br/>a single segment is just its secant"]

    P5["<b>STAGE 1 — interior tangents</b>  :196-211<br/>for i in 1 .. n-2:<br/><br/>if d[i-1] x d[i] &lt;= 0:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>m[i] = 0</b> — the secants disagree in<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;sign, so an EXTREMUM sits on this knot<br/>else:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;h0 = x[i] - x[i-1], h1 = x[i+1] - x[i]<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;w0 = 2 h1 + h0, w1 = h1 + 2 h0<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>m[i] = w0 + w1 / w0/d[i-1] + w1/d[i]</b><br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;weighted HARMONIC mean of adjacent<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;secants — provably monotone-preserving"]

    P6["<b>STAGE 1 — endpoints</b>  :214-215<br/>m[0]   = EndpointTangent d0,d1,h0,h1<br/>m[n-1] = EndpointTangent d n-2, d n-3, ...<br/>one-sided three-point estimate<br/>de Boor, A Practical Guide to Splines"]

    P7["<b>EndpointTangent d0, d1, h0, h1</b>  :250-262<br/>m = 2 h0 + h1 x d0 - h0 x d1 / h0 + h1<br/><br/>CLAMP 1 :255 — if m x d0 &lt;= 0 return 0<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;opposite sign to the nearer secant means<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;an extremum sits on the endpoint<br/>CLAMP 2 :258 — if d0 x d1 &lt;= 0 and<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;abs m &gt; abs 3 d0 return 3 d0"]

    P8["<b>STAGE 2 — Fritsch-Carlson clamp</b>  :220-241<br/>the sufficient condition for monotonicity<br/>for i in 0 .. n-2:<br/><br/>if d[i] == 0:  :222<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;m[i] = m[i+1] = 0 — a FLAT segment;<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;any nonzero tangent would overshoot<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;the constant value<br/>else:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;alpha = m[i] / d[i]<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;beta  = m[i+1] / d[i]<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;r = alpha^2 + beta^2<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>if r &gt; 9:</b>  :235<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;tau = 3 / sqrt r<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;m[i]   = tau x alpha x d[i]<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;m[i+1] = tau x beta  x d[i]<br/><br/>r &gt; 9 is the circle of radius 3 in<br/>alpha-beta space — outside it, monotonicity<br/>is not guaranteed, so scale back onto it"]

    P9["<b>Evaluate t</b>  :105-127<br/>t &lt;= x[0]   -> y[0]      constant extrapolation<br/>t &gt;= x[n-1] -> y[n-1]<br/>i = FindSegment t  binary search :156-167<br/>h = x[i+1] - x[i],  s = t - x[i] / h<br/><br/><b>cubic Hermite basis</b>  :118-121<br/>h00 = 2 s^3 - 3 s^2 + 1<br/>h10 = s^3 - 2 s^2 + s<br/>h01 = -2 s^3 + 3 s^2<br/>h11 = s^3 - s^2<br/><br/><b>p = h00 y[i] + h10 h m[i]<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;+ h01 y[i+1] + h11 h m[i+1]</b>  :123-126"]

    P10["<b>Derivative t</b>  :133-153<br/>outside the range -> 0  flat extrapolation<br/><br/>dh00 = 6 s^2 - 6 s / h<br/>dh10 = 3 s^2 - 4 s + 1<br/>dh01 = -6 s^2 + 6 s / h<br/>dh11 = 3 s^2 - 2 s<br/><br/>p' = dh00 y[i] + dh10 m[i]<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;+ dh01 y[i+1] + dh11 m[i+1]<br/><br/>zero-crossings of THIS are the extrema<br/>that ExtremaDetector hunts"]

    P0 --> P1 --> P2 --> P3
    P3 -- yes --> P4
    P3 -- no --> P5 --> P6 --> P8
    P6 -.-> P7
    P8 --> P9
    P8 --> P10
end

%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------
%% 5b. HEMISPHERE NORMALISATION
%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------
subgraph SIGN["5b · QuaternionSignNorm — the double-cover trap · QuaternionSignNorm.cs"]
    direction TB
    Q1["<b>The problem</b>  :9-13<br/>q and -q encode the SAME rotation but sit on<br/>opposite hemispheres of the 4-sphere.<br/>Per-component interpolation between<br/>hemisphere-inconsistent samples takes the<br/>LONG PATH — a roughly 360 deg detour —<br/>and PCHIP reproduces it faithfully,<br/>producing a visible spin spike."]
    Q2["<b>Normalise q, count</b>  :41-51<br/>for i in 1 .. count-1:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;if Quaternion.Dot q[i-1], q[i] &lt; 0:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;q[i] = -q[i].x, -y, -z, -w<br/><br/>first sample is the canonical reference;<br/>each later one is negated if it would<br/>otherwise take the long way round"]
    Q3["<b>Consequence for bit-identity</b>  :18-21<br/>this may NEGATE the newest sample before<br/>fitting. Evaluate at the newest knot then<br/>returns -q: same rotation, different bits.<br/>Measured: an exact negation about 47 pct of<br/>the time on inconsistent input."]
    Q1 --> Q2 --> Q3
end

%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------
%% 6. EXTREMA DETECTION
%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------
subgraph EXTREMA["6 · ExtremaDetector — Brent 1973 root finding · ExtremaDetector.cs"]
    direction TB

    E1["<b>FindForBone sampler, tStart, tEnd, results, dt = 0.016</b>  :48<br/>results.Clear; bail if tEnd &lt;= tStart<br/>scratch list is <b>ThreadStatic</b> :38 — a public<br/>static utility with a shared mutable buffer<br/>would corrupt silently under a worker thread"]

    E2["<b>SCAN — one fused pass over all four components</b>  :63-82<br/>prev = sampler.Derivative tStart<br/>for t = tStart + dt; t &lt;= tEnd + 1e-6; t += dt:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;t = min t, tEnd<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;curr = sampler.Derivative t<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;for c in 0 .. 3:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>if prev[c] x curr[c] &lt; 0</b> -> sign change<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;brackets a zero crossing on component c<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-> all.Add Brent sampler, c, tPrev, t<br/><br/>all four components in ONE pass: Derivative<br/>evaluates all four regardless, so scanning them<br/>separately discarded three quarters of every<br/>result. A bone extremum occurs when ANY<br/>component's derivative hits zero."]

    E3["<b>Brent sampler, component, a, b</b>  :112-180<br/>BrentTol = 1e-4 :26 · BrentMaxIter = 50 :27<br/><br/>fa, fb = derivative at the bracket ends<br/>if fa x fb &gt; 0 -> midpoint fallback :117-118<br/>ensure abs fa &gt;= abs fb, else swap :120-124<br/><br/>loop until abs b - a &lt; tol or 50 iterations:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;if fa != fc and fb != fc:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>inverse quadratic interpolation</b> :138-140<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;else:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>secant method</b> :145<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;five acceptance conditions :148-154<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;if any fails -> <b>bisection fallback</b> :158<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;re-bracket on the sign of fa x fs :169-170<br/><br/>guaranteed convergence, superlinear near<br/>the root — bisection's safety with the<br/>speed of interpolation"]

    E4{"all.Count == 0 ?<br/>:84"}
    E5["return — no extrema this window"]
    E6["all.Sort  :86"]

    E7["<b>MERGE ACROSS COMPONENTS</b>  :91-96<br/>MinSegment = 0.016  :31  ~1 frame at 60 Hz<br/>for each e in sorted order:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;if results empty OR<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;e - last &gt;= MinSegment -> keep<br/><br/>two components crossing zero a fraction of a<br/>millisecond apart describe the SAME turning<br/>point. Below one frame they are numerically<br/>indistinguishable anyway.<br/><br/>this tolerance is what :313-323 in the<br/>scheduler mirrors when it dedupes candidates."]

    E1 --> E2 --> E4
    E2 -.-> E3
    E4 -- yes --> E5
    E4 -- no --> E6 --> E7
end

%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------
%% 7. PROXY DECOUPLING
%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------
subgraph PROXY["7 · RagdollProxyBuilder — why physics needs a clone · RagdollProxyBuilder.cs"]
    direction TB

    X0["<b>THE CATEGORY ERROR THIS AVOIDS</b>  :9-15<br/>Writing localRotation onto a non-kinematic<br/>Rigidbody under a CharacterJoint makes the<br/>joint think the bone drifted from its<br/>constraint target. The solver pushes back, and<br/>that corrective impulse ACCUMULATES every<br/>FixedUpdate. Bodies that should fall under<br/>gravity accelerate sideways.<br/><br/>Sequential-impulse solvers already run a FIXED<br/>iteration count and converge slowly on deep<br/>ragdoll tree topology. Injecting an externally<br/>authored pose is not adding noise to a stable<br/>process — it is forcing a process already<br/>fighting to stay converged."]

    X1["<b>Build source, stripComponents, ...</b>  :38<br/>clone = Instantiate source at same pos/rot,<br/><b>parent = null</b>  :46-47"]

    X2["<b>Why scene root, not a child</b>  :31-36<br/>if the proxy were parented to the source,<br/>anything that disables or destroys the source<br/>— pooling, hit reactions, dismemberment —<br/>would take the proxy with it. Scene root<br/>means the proxy outlives the source."]

    X3["clone.SetActive false  :49<br/>BEFORE any component can Awake"]

    X4["<b>DestroyImmediate every IOnTwosComponent</b>  :57<br/>Instantiate copies OUR components too, so<br/>without this the clone would try to build its<br/>own proxy — infinite recursion, mitigated only<br/>by Destroy's end-of-frame timing.<br/>DestroyImmediate on an INACTIVE object is safe<br/>and has no frame-ordering side effects."]

    X5["<b>StripToRenderersOnly</b>  :121-142<br/>DestroyImmediate, in this order:<br/>Joint -> Rigidbody -> Collider<br/>-> MonoBehaviour -> Animator<br/><br/>joints before bodies so Unity resolves the<br/>CharacterJoint to Rigidbody dependency itself"]

    X6["clone.SetActive true  :62<br/>force-enable renderers  :64-78<br/>SkinnedMeshRenderer.updateWhenOffscreen = true<br/>— stripped scripts may have run OnDisable and<br/>left renderers off"]

    X7["<b>PATH-BASED BONE PAIRING</b>  :83-106<br/>sourceBodies = GetComponentsInChildren Rigidbody<br/>BonePathCache over the clone  :84<br/>for each source body:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;proxyBone = paths.Find sourceRoot, rb.transform<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;pair them, or warn and skip<br/><br/>matched by HIERARCHY PATH, not by index —<br/>index pairing breaks the moment a limb is<br/>destroyed and the arrays are rebuilt"]

    X8["<b>RESULT</b><br/>SourceBodies — physics, untouched, still solving<br/>VisualBones  — render-only, no physics at all<br/><br/>RagdollStepper reads the first and writes the<br/>second. The stylisation NEVER enters the<br/>solver's state, which is the architectural<br/>claim of the whole project."]

    X0 --> X1 --> X3 --> X4 --> X5 --> X6 --> X7 --> X8
    X1 -.-> X2
end

